<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ieb8745a0d9100cfa1a5d4d89911710dd9ce5bc7a" commit="0550429016eea8df1d16467820e32aca8f1a28c5" commit_message="authpolicy: Periodically change machine password  Runs a service in authpolicyd that periodically checks the password age and renews it if it's older than 30 days by default (can be customized with the DeviceMachinePasswordChangeRate policy). Password renewal helps increase security (hackers have less time to brute force a password) and it helps Active Directory admins to clear out stale machine accounts.  Keeps the old machine password around and uses that for kinit in case the current password fails. This is important for large Active Directory deployments where the machine password might not have propagated through Active Directory yet after a password change, but the old one is still accepted (could use propagation retry alternatively, but that's slower).  CQ-DEPEND=CL:921622,CL:913409  BUG=chromium:777979,chromium:815139 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=amd64-generic --packages authpolicy  Change-Id: Ieb8745a0d9100cfa1a5d4d89911710dd9ce5bc7a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/924123 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="924123" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/23/924123/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia2d3cc04fd2dc2664b08cda111bc7e59e88b37fc" commit="1eeabc5f020ceed455676f5b75e2ed4fb3a2cee4" commit_message="authpolicy: Send machine password via stdin  Sends the machine password during domain join via stdin instead of using command line args. The args are visible in ps, which is a security issue.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:934446  BUG=chromium:777979 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=amd64-generic --packages authpolicy      Tested on device  Change-Id: Ia2d3cc04fd2dc2664b08cda111bc7e59e88b37fc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/951690 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Roman Sorokin &lt;rsorokin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="951690" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/90/951690/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaf15b10c4481094d6d0b5d097bcc3bf03ac3181f" commit="a596efa478104b8962902fd67013f2a539f8420f" commit_message="Samba: Don't set PasswordNeverExpires flag  Does not set the PasswordNeverExpires flag (0x10000 in userAccountControl in net ads search result) on newly created machine accounts. The flag prevents machine account passwords from ever expiring. However, this is a security issue and CL:924123 adds the ability to authpolicyd to roll the machine password periodically, so the flag is not needed anymore.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:924123  BUG=chromium:777979 TEST=Ran net ads join on device and made sure that PasswordNeverExpires      is not set. Alternatively, one could also domain join Chromebook      and check the value of userAccountControl value in machine      account LDAP attribute editor in Windows.  Change-Id: Iaf15b10c4481094d6d0b5d097bcc3bf03ac3181f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/955424 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="955424" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/